            <ArticleTitle>Retrograde embolization after balloon angioplasty in a patient with late stent subthrombosis in a paclitaxel-eluting stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>797-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a 65-year-old patient who underwent a semi-urgent percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) for a very late stent subthrombosis (13 months) in a paclitaxel-eluting stent (PES) while still on dual antiplatelet therapy.The procedure was complicated by a retrograde embolization into the circumflex artery (CFX). We will focus on the risk of distal embolization after primary PCI for acute stent thrombosis and its prevention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
